      "id": "C01-01",
      "subtitles_zh": "大军出发的时候，最容易记住的是那个很大的总人数。但到接战以前，还有一整段路。军队要带着补给，经过不同地点，可能减少兵员，也可能得到补充。到了战场，还剩多少人、有没有补给、能不能及时加入，不能只靠出发时的一个数字回答。",
      "subtitles_en": "When a large army sets out, its total soldier count is easy to remember. But there is a whole journey before it joins the battle. It carries supplies through different places, and may lose soldiers or receive reinforcement along the way. That starting number alone cannot tell us how many soldiers will arrive, whether they will have supplies, or whether they can join in time.",
